---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { PARTS, PEERS } from "../data/landscape.js";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <header class="top">
    <span class="top-meta">lifeos · research notes · v0</span>
    <nav class="top-nav" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#scene">scene</a>
      <a href="#bundle">bundle</a>
      <a href="#field">field</a>
      <a href="#lifeos">lifeos</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/Angelguirao/meta-harness">source</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <div class="hero-bleed" aria-hidden="true">
    <pre class="schematic"><code>┌─ shop ──────────────────────────────────────┐
│  continuity   scope   constraint   work     │
│  retrieve     swap                          │
│       │                                     │
│       ▼                                     │
│  ┌─ muscle ─────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  claude code · codex · deep agents   │   │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────┘   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>
  </div>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1 class="brand">meta-harness</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Working name for the shop above the coding agent — the stuff that
        survives when the chat dies.
      </p>
      <p class="dek">
        Not a product pitch. Notes from running
        <a href="https://github.com/Angelguirao/personal-ai-os">LifeOS</a>
        next to everyone else who is building this layer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="scene" id="scene" aria-labelledby="scene-title">
      <h2 id="scene-title">Tuesday, still broken</h2>
      <p>
        Ticket: cancel a stuck order. Needs the payments API, the customer web
        app, and a design-system confirm dialog. Three repos. Claude Code can
        edit one tree at a time. You clone, branch, paste context, babysit
        three PRs so they land in the same deploy.
      </p>
      <p>
        Last Thursday you already decided retries belong in the gateway — in a
        chat that is gone. The branch has the patch. Nothing queryable has the
        decision. Your other laptop burned the same afternoon yesterday.
      </p>
      <p class="punch">
        That gap is the category. Better prompts are not it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="define" aria-labelledby="define-title">
      <h2 id="define-title">Working definition</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>harness</strong> is one agent loop in one session — Claude
        Code, Codex, Deep Agents. A <strong>meta-harness</strong>, as we use
        the word here, is not a single SKU. It is a
        <strong>bundle of organs</strong> that make those loops usable across
        time, repos, and risk: continuity, scope, constraint, work graph,
        retrieve, swap.
      </p>
      <p>
        Peers ship different subsets hard.
        <a href="https://metaharness.tools">metaharness.tools</a> is a useful
        map of the conversation — not our dictionary. We learn the label by
        placing LifeOS next to the field.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bundle" id="bundle" aria-labelledby="bundle-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="bundle-title">If this organ is missing</h2>
        <p>Each line is a failure mode, not a feature slogan.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="matrix">
        {
          PARTS.map((part) => (
            <li>
              <span class="matrix-id">{part.label}</span>
              <span class="matrix-blurb">{part.miss}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="field" id="field" aria-labelledby="field-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="field-title">Field notes</h2>
        <p>Center of gravity — who owns which organ hard.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="owners-wrap">
        <table class="owners">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Name</th>
              <th scope="col">Owns hard</th>
              <th scope="col">Read as</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              PEERS.map((p) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">
                    {p.url ? (
                      <a href={p.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                        {p.name}
                      </a>
                    ) : (
                      p.name
                    )}
                  </th>
                  <td class="owns">{p.owns}</td>
                  <td>{p.note}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="note">
        <mark>Cerebras Knowledge</mark> is retrieve done well. It can sit inside
        a fuller stack. Continuity + scope + constraint are still someone
        else’s job — same pattern as a tracker that only does work, or a
        sandbox that only does constraint.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="lifeos" id="lifeos" aria-labelledby="lifeos-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="lifeos-title">Where LifeOS sits</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/Angelguirao/personal-ai-os">personal-ai-os</a>
          — what we actually run, not what we wish we shipped.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cut" role="group" aria-label="LifeOS inventory">
        <div class="cut-row">
          <span class="cut-k">heavy today</span>
          <span class="cut-v"
            >world model (folio · ledger · trackers) · OPEVL walker · Work /
            Run / Session coordination</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="cut-row">
          <span class="cut-k">muscle</span>
          <span class="cut-v"
            >Fly Deep Agents; Claude Code / Codex optional — swappable in
            doctrine, sticky in practice</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="cut-row">
          <span class="cut-k">thin</span>
          <span class="cut-v"
            >cross-repo scope · session handoff that agents trust · OS-level
            sandbox</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="cut-row cut-row-open">
          <span class="cut-k">open bet</span>
          <span class="cut-v"
            >which thin gap becomes the product — or whether the asset is the
            world model that dispatches wraps</span
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">
        Working thesis: control plane + world model first. Meta-harness organs
        attach as substrates for Session and Run — not a rename, not a claim
        that we are Omnigent.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="open" aria-labelledby="open-title">
      <h2 id="open-title">Still open</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          After a cross-repo cancel-order, what should still be queryable next
          Tuesday without re-explaining?
        </li>
        <li>
          If we only harden one thin organ next, is it handoff, sandbox, or
          scope?
        </li>
        <li>
          Would we still need LifeOS if Omnigent + Beads + a knowledge organ
          covered the week — or is the world model the irreplaceable piece?
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="foot">
    <p>
      Written beside LifeOS. Labels move. MIT ·
      <a href="https://github.com/Angelguirao/meta-harness">source</a>
    </p>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
